  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $\u2016v\u2016=7$ and $\u20162u+v\u2016=25.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $\u2016u\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20162u+v{\u2016}^{2} & =\u20162u{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v{\u2016}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u20162u+v{\u2016}^{2} & =(2\u2016u\u2016)^{2}+\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ \u20162u+v{\u2016}^{2} & =4\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+\u2016v{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =4\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+(7)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =4\u2016u{\u2016}^{2}+49 \\\\ 576 & =4\u2016u{\u2016}^{2} \\\\ \u2016u{\u2016}^{2} & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\u2016u\u2016=12.$",
